Suggested Calendar Treatment
Use only the short Calendar card text in the visible week. The expanded material should appear after selection, alongside the mode and area labels.

To keep the page readable:

Display 3–4 entries per day.

Use color primarily for operating mode, not for every functional category.

Show functional areas as text labels inside the expanded state.

Allow an entry to belong to several areas, reinforcing the interconnected nature of the role.

On mobile, convert the grid into a five-day vertical agenda with notes expanding inline.

Include a permanent disclaimer such as: “An illustrative composite showing the range of work within the role; not a record of a particular week.”